speechtext:
1.	How many gallons of spirits have been sold outside of Canada, (a) to the United States;
(b)	to the United Kingdom; (c) to others, during each of the years 1939, 1940, 1941, 1942, 1943?
2.	How many gallons of beer have been sold outside of Canada, (a) to the United States; (b) to the United Kingdom; (c) to others, during each of the years 1939, 1940, 1941, 1942, 1943?

The discussion must of necessity be generalized in a way, although it was understood-I am in the hands of the committee and have no power to dictate to it __that members of the committee, in their discussion, would keep very closely to the items and department before the chair. So far this dine of conduct or understanding has been

]Var Appropriation-Supplies
pretty well followed, and it should be fairly easy for the members of the committee to follow this precedent so as to keep within the limits of the item as much as possible. I must also make this statement. You must realize how hard it is for the chair not to rule in favour of the minister-
